course: dictionary
lesson: 11722
title: Who wrote it? Authorship
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Authorship means being the person who wrote a book, article, song or other piece of work. «The authorship of this poem is clear: the name at the top is Amara Hughes.» The writer of a text is its author, and the author's name tells us the authorship.
explain: Sometimes authorship is not certain, so it becomes a question: who wrote this? «The authorship of the old letter is disputed, because nobody can prove who wrote it.» Disputed means people argue about it and do not agree.
explain: Authorship can also be shared. «The song had joint authorship: two friends wrote the words and the music together.» Joint means shared. To check a meaning, put your idea into the sentence: does «the authorship of the song» still make sense as "who wrote the song"? If yes, you have it.
fact: Authorship means who wrote a piece of work.
fact: «Author» is the person who writes, and «authorship» is the fact of being that person.
fact: «Disputed authorship» means people do not agree on who wrote something.
fact: «Joint authorship» means two or more people wrote the work together.
fact: Authorship usually has no plural, so we say «the authorship», not «the authorships».
exercise: «The authorship of the book is printed on the cover.» What does authorship mean here? | Who sells the book | Where the book was printed | How many pages the book has | *Who wrote the book
exercise: «The authorship of the letter is disputed, so nobody is sure who wrote it.» What does disputed mean? | People have read it aloud | People agree on it completely | *People argue about it | People have lost it
exercise: «The song had joint authorship.» What does joint mean? | Written in pencil | *Shared between two or more people | Very old | Sung very loudly
test: «Maya claimed authorship of the poem, but her teacher was not sure.» What does claimed authorship mean? | Said she had read it twice | Said she had lost the poem | *Said she was the one who wrote it | Said she would sing it at assembly
test: Which phrase means two people wrote a song together? | Disputed authorship | Ancient authorship | *Joint authorship | Authorship of a castle
exam: What does authorship mean in «The authorship of the diary is uncertain»? | The colour of the diary cover | *The question of who wrote the diary | The number of pages in the diary | The date the diary was bought
